## The Core Problem (diagnosed and resolved analytically)
User came in reporting a traffic drop: rankings, impressions, and clicks down on web search; image search traffic comparatively stable.

### Diagnosis process (using two GSC exports the user uploaded):
- File 1: Aug 1-24, 2026 (before period, 24 days)
- File 2: Aug 25-Sep 6, 2026 (after period, 13 days)
- Aggregate: clicks dropped ~70%, impressions dropped ~60% comparing daily averages
- Initial hypothesis: seasonal decay (August-named pages like "end-of-summer-nails" naturally dying as month ended) — confirmed as a real contributing factor, biggest single page loss was `/blog/end-of-summer-nails`
- BUT: further analysis of evergreen (non-seasonal) pages showed they ALSO lost position and impressions significantly (e.g. `simple-nail-designs` dropped from position ~10.5 to ~35.4; `pedicure-cost`, `gel-nails-cost`, `nail-tools-and-prep` all lost 70-98% impressions)
- 161 pages dropped position by more than 3 spots; only 12 improved — broad, one-directional site-wide hit, not random
- Cross-referenced with Google's confirmed August 2026 Spam Update (rolled out Aug 18-21, 2026, per Google's Search Status Dashboard) — timing is a few days off from the user's Aug 24-25 drop start, but the pattern (whole topic clusters like `nail-basics`, `simple-nail-designs`, `coffin-nails`, `history-of-nails` collapsing together) is the classic signature of a spam/helpful-content-style update evaluating content clusters, not individual pages
- **Conclusion: this is a real algorithmic quality/spam-update hit layered on top of natural seasonal decay, not seasonal decay alone.**

